WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
A seaside town keeps two
sets of monthly figures.

2
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:05.690
One is ice-cream sales.

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.830
The other is drownings.

4
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.610
Plot them against each
other, one point per month,

5
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.560
and the points climb steadily
from bottom left to top right.

6
00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.410
The correlation coefficient comes
out at nought point eight seven.

7
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.200
So should the town ban ice cream?

8
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.010
Does one of these really cause the other?

9
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.480
In this mission, you'll describe
scatter diagrams as positive,

10
00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:31.850
negative or no correlation,
and as strong or weak.

11
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.750
You'll find Pearson's r on your GDC, and
see that it always lies between minus

12
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.200
one and one.

13
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:42.250
And you'll learn what a correlation
can, and can't, tell you.

14
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.520
Your mission: decide whether ice
cream really causes drownings.
